--- /dev/null
+++ b/SM-T311-G1012-RELEASE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+# SM-T311 G1012 - G1002 physically accepted decoder on active Codec2 source branch
+
+This source tree on branch sm-t311-q31m-v4l2-codec2 was fast-forwarded from previously physically installed G975 (a4ef67b) to code lineage 042c008, 722a610, 33605d2 on 2026-10-23 after guarded physical acceptance of the H.264 decoder.
+
+Specific change: on lt013g when visible hardware H.264 decoder geometry is 640 x 1024, request the firmware-advertised 14 MFC CAPTURE DPB buffers instead of G975 18 (MIN_BUFFERS_FOR_CAPTURE+4), and at most 8 downstream Codec2 display BufferQueue blocks instead of 14/18. Hardware FIMC remains in the DMA conversion path. The 1280x720 coded 1280x736 pathway uses original 15 capture/display allocations without reduction. All encoder modes, radio, camera/audio source, BOOT, recovery and kernel source are unchanged by this commit.
+
+Physical tested exact ARM32 library (permanent SYSTEM/vendor/lib install G1012):
+f735ad9ed95bff53eb0f928476b61b27f9875e23465f3f196bfe5d24877dd7c9
+Original G975 rollback library:
+6137f22dad0e0d7670020d50fb86266c7755b24dd546cb7ce3830a2bb89f75f6
+
+Hardware quality gates previously observed:
+- G1002 short 640x1024 complete drain 394 frames.
+- G1003/G1005 same portrait long 125s, 2316 decoded frames and no reported drops; entire 301s video not played.
+- G1010 full 1280x720 72s hardware 2154 FIMC frames Q29L_DRAIN_COMPLETE; NuPlayer reported 2155 frames, 0 drops, AAC audio.
+- G1011 same HAL hot switch 640x1024 portrait 576 frames, zero dropped -> 1280x720 full hardware drain 2154, NuPlayer 2155 frames, **1 dropped on switch**. No during-playback codec timeout.
+- G1008/G1009 alternative BQ-only periodic polling physically rejected 44 frames / 6651ms; not included in this source.
+- G1006 increased CMA160 alone physically rejected; kernel G958 original CMA128 remains.
+
+G1012 signed Codec2-only TWRP install and restore source lives under project linux-7.3-port/tools/g1012-codec2-signed-twrp-only.py, manifest in linux-7.3-port/G1012_CODECONLY_TWRP_PACKAGE_MANIFEST.json. Install physically flashed only Codec2 via TWRP3.1.1, verified exact SHA from mounted SYSTEM in recovery, then Android rebooted (boot_completed=1, SELinux Enforcing, Codec2 HAL, RIL, SurfaceFlinger running) and exact library SHA independently read back. Original RIL, BOOT, TWRP unchanged, no backups.
+
+IMPORTANT LIMITATIONS: screenrecord H264 portrait bitstream remains intermittently corrupted, independent of decoder; camera 720p AAC previously passes. With this buffer policy, CMA may have CmaFree~0KB during media playback, no proven OOM but also no reserve; continue reviewing memory allocation pressure. A 1-frame drop happened on hot switching to 720p. Encoder corruption and force-stop FLUSHING error are NOT declared fixed. Real telephone/SMS, USB and GNSS open; do not claim total device ready.
+
+Host reproducibility: G1012 private isolated rebuild built a different ELF SHA due .gnu_debugdata and build-ID; loadable .text/.rodata/dynamic sections matched byte-for-byte. Do not use rebuilt ELF for release without re-testing. The staged candidate artifact is an exact copy of the physically tested SHA. The signed restore G975 ZIP is always available. Maintain g960 exact source/built lock and g994 physical release snapshot: full ROM/RIL MUST remain blocked because host rebuilt libril bb1e67... does not equal original installed 4e6bb8a9. User publishes GitHub personally, never push.
+
+Current permanent device expected:
+- Codec2 f735ad9ed95bff53eb0f928476b61b27f9875e23465f3f196bfe5d24877dd7c9
+- BOOT e42c1b09b4c4d3c91b1a3c5330619d37560287821994d269ba67a970069cd5fd
+- TWRP f818c29f65d2082cb642cac85e27715c5255c87aac627bb542b777129d4f784f
+- RIL 4e6bb8a9465005a01f5bebd92a7e0ad247c0c4b609809c2600547bc97999bcb7
+
+Do not rerun completed physical QA; commit source changes and preserve historical ledger.
